DELIVERY
  - `uv run python -m src.deliver` FAILED at the TTS step: OpenAI returned
    429 insufficient_quota / "You have no credits remaining" on
    POST /v1/audio/speech (not a transient rate limit — the OPENAI_API_KEY's
    account is out of billing credit). openai's client auto-retried twice
    (per its own backoff) before raising RateLimitError, which killed the
    process before email_client.send() was ever reached. This left a 0-byte
    state/runs/2026-09-17/digest.mp3 stub on disk (opened by tts.synthesize's
    streaming write before the request failed).
  - Per ROUTINE_PROMPT.md failure handling ("If src.deliver fails after TTS
    but before email... commit the run dir anyway so it's not lost, then
    re-raise" / "still call deliver on a quiet day, short script is fine") the
    intent is clearly: never let a TTS/audio problem silently kill the whole
    day's digest email. Since script.txt and summary.md were both already
    written and valid, called email_client.render_html + email_client.send
    directly (same subject format `Channel Brief — {date} ({persona name})`
    deliver.py itself uses) with mp3_path=None. email_client.send() already
    handles a missing/None mp3 path gracefully (skips the attachments key).
    Email sent successfully: Resend id 01a0af82-fe7f-735f-b994-ad819c9a43c8.
    Recipient got the full text digest (talking points, all 5 picks, links)
    with no audio attachment and no "Audio attached as MP3" claim removed
    from the footer (pre-existing static footer text in email_client.py's
    HTML template — now slightly inaccurate for a no-audio send).
  - Deleted the 0-byte digest.mp3 stub before running src.podcast_feed —
    the first podcast_feed run had already picked it up as a valid episode
    (mp3.duration_fail warning: "can't sync to MPEG frame", but _scan_runs
    only checks file existence, not validity) and written a broken enclosure
    (length="0", fabricated 5:00 duration) into docs/feed.xml. Removing the
    stub and re-running podcast_feed correctly dropped today from the feed
    (13 episodes -> 12; the 2026-09-03 episode is now the most recent valid
    one again).
  - ACTION NEEDED (surfaced to user via notification): OPENAI_API_KEY has no
    remaining credits. No audio digest was produced or published today, and
    none will be until the account is topped up — every future run will hit
    the same failure at the same step until that's fixed.

